mothershipOS (mship.video): HEVC codec config in front of the first picture. Venus (SM8250, VIDEO.VPU.1.0-00119)
drops an HEVC buffer that holds only headers (VPS/SPS/PPS/SEI, i.e. the codec config Android sends first): no
source change, no buffer back, the decoder waits forever. A buffer without a coded picture (no VCL NAL unit) is now
completed at once and its bytes go in front of the next picture's (as players that prepend extradata do); the last
headers are prepended again after a flush, which restarts the stream. H.264 takes header-only buffers and is left
as it is.

--- a/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.h
+++ b/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.h
@@ -126,6 +126,12 @@
     // mothershipOS: the visible rectangle of the last key frame / SPS seen in the bitstream. Venus firmware does not
     // always report crop information: its compose rectangle is then the coded size (1920x1088 for 1080p).
     std::optional<Rect> mStreamVisibleRect;
+
+    // mothershipOS: HEVC buffers without a picture (parameter sets, SEI: the codec config) wait here for the next
+    // picture, which carries them; Venus drops a buffer with headers only. The last ones are kept to go in front of
+    // the first picture after a flush.
+    std::vector<uint8_t> mHevcPrefix;
+    std::vector<uint8_t> mHevcHeaders;
     // Holds information about secure playback, which won't allow decoder to
     // access frames in order to provide extra meta information (like checking
     // for pending DRC).
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,16 @@
